      "Language": "tur",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Morton neuroma is a paroxysmal neuralgia form pain usually occurs at the 3rd finger and sole of the foot. The patient mostly suffer from pain while walking. In this report a 40-year-old man with Morton neuroma who has a stress fracture in the other leg because of not using the affected painful foot."},
